error[VLT0120]: a `=>` here is a bound clause, and this is not one
  --> bound_clause_shape.vlt:21:24
   |
21 | shout : Into<String> t => t -> String
   |                        ^^
  = help: doc 18 §2.2 reads a bound as a trait and the variable it bounds, each a bare name: `Ord t =>`, or `Ord t, Clone t =>`. A trait with type arguments (`Into<String> t`), a path on the left (`Clone i::IntoIter`), a `?Sized`, and a bound between two lifetimes are all out of reach — `docs/GRAMMAR.md` grades them, and inline Rust is the hatch

